   "source": [
    "## Question 1 ##"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "205adbe2-c5f9-4022-9d76-dcdeb6b3e8dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Initially, this algorithm was implemented by using a for loop. However, in later questions, I realised this became quite computationally expensive and inefficient, therefore I have now implemented a vectorized approach for improved efficiency. I used previous problem sheets to help me with this."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "f6d10356-72e9-40c9-96d4-58176ed7c7c6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def grad_loss(Xh, Theta, Y):\n",
    "    N = np.shape(Xh)[0]\n",
    "    Xh_with_bias = extend_X(Xh)\n",
    "    H = h(Xh, Theta) # here we have the computation (h(xi)-yi). funtion h(Xh, Theta) is as defined above, which computes the matrix of probabilities that point i is in class j\n",
    "    grad_loss = (np.transpose(Xh_with_bias)@(H-Y))/N \n",
    "    return grad_loss"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "552d098e-decc-481f-9fc5-ebdb21e9a1a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "test_grad1()\n",
    "test_grad2()\n",
    "test_grad3()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa75aa0e-5a00-4ca3-86df-548ac3fcdbdb",
