   "source": [
    "Initial output gave thetastar as still an array of 0s. Having looked at the array of losses, I realised that the agd() function had a learning rate t which was too large, resulting in the function not converging, and instead overstepping and diverging. Hence I have now written the following code to find a t value which will allow agd to converge, while not taking steps that are too small and therefore inefficient (and may not converge before the function hits the max number of iterations S)"
   ]
