   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After running this code a few times, generally t=0.25 seems to give the best learning rate, as it provides the best trade off between accuracy of convergence and number of iterations. With smaller values of t, we find that the steps are too small, and the function takes too long to compute, and larger values we don't get effective convergence to the optimal parameter, leading to all the points being classified into the same class"
   ]
